{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 120,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Macroeconomics has not been successful\nfor 200 years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2920,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I’ve noticed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3920,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Exactly.\nIt's been a failure for 200 years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5720,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No progress."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6760,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think most economic ideas are bad ideas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10080,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If t here's a group of people"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11040,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that I can't stand,\nit is economists driving me up the wall."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14960,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mainly in a career,\nI say don't do an economics degree."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17520,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bashing economics, especially on popular"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20280,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "podcasts like Lex Fridman or Tucker\nCarlson."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23440,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Can get you hundreds of thousands,\nif not millions of views."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28080,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But are these criticisms fair,\nor are they just"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32080,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sensationalist nonsense\nthat's used to get views?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35680,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey, I'm Joeri, I have a Ph.D."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37400,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in economics and I used to teach economics\nat several universities."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40800,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And today my employee, Alejandro here"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45480,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who is also an economist, has selected\nseveral popular video"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48400,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "clips with people ranging from professors\nto YouTubers to investors"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52280,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "-bashing economics for me to react to."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55280,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as I understood it, these criticisms\nessentially come in three flavors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61160,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number one,\neconomics is not a hard or a real science."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64640,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number two,\neconomic models are terribly outdated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67280,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And number three, don't study\neconomics, It's a waste of time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72240,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is how Alejandro\nordered the clips for me."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74320,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's get into criticism type\nnumber one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77760,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Economists make bad predictions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80400,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not a hard or real science."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83800,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know\neconomics is not a physical science."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85680,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's no way for me to go"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87080,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and do an experiment and say here,\nlet's let's run the Covid economy again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91360,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But with taxation on the rich and show\nhigh living standards, you bet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94480,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can't do that physical experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96120,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All we can do is predict."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97560,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that is why banks pay millions\nof pounds a year to good predictors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101160,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because that's the best way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102480,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to tell who's a good economist,\nbecause we can't do physical experiments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105480,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it drives me mad that these economists\nwho make policy and protect policy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109920,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that protects them and their class\nand the rich don't even accept"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114720,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when somebody consistently predicts them,\nthey won't even listen to you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118200,
    "dDurationMs": 640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Drives me mad."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118840,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, so popular YouTuber Gary,\nan ex-trader makes two claims here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124960,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Economics is not as good\nas physical sciences."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128080,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And number two,\nso this critique is not entirely true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131000,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To make financial market predictions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132640,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And therefore\nhe is actually a really good economist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135560,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet economists like me\ndo not listen to him."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138840,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, I see variants of these"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141440,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "two claims actually a lot\nin the comment section on this channel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144920,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Economics is not a very good science,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146560,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you should really listen\nto rich investors rather than economists."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150480,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let me just address both of these once\nand for all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155400,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For the first claim,\nI actually half agree with Gary."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159600,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Economics is a social science\nwhich is less"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162480,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "good than a physical or hard science."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166440,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's play a part of that clip again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168800,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you know,\neconomics is not a physical science."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170800,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's no way for me to go"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172200,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and do an experiment and say, here,\nlet's let's run the Covid economy again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176320,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here,\nhe gets to an absolutely crucial point"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178800,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about why economists, and especially macro\neconomists, can never get to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185160,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this scientific gold standard of doing\ncontrol experiments in the laboratory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189480,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, that's the half that I agree with."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192320,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm pretty envious that,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193320,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for example, chemists can do super control\nexperiments in a lab."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197040,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, this is much harder\nfor social scientists like economists"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200440,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like me, but also sociologists\nor political scientists."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204360,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I would argue that not being able\nto do laboratory experiments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208320,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is actually a problem for many,\nmany natural systems as well,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213000,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "given that they're big enough\nnot to fit in lab right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216480,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gary's Covid\neconomy is a macroeconomic phenomena."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220000,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you just look at the UK\nlike Gary tends to do,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222680,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that means that we're talking\nabout millions of individuals,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224880,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "millions of firms, hundreds of banks\ninteracting with government"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228280,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the central bank, as well as,\nof course, other countries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231280,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You cannot put the entire UK inside\na laboratory to do a controlled experiment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236200,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to compare the differences"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237200,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between doing Covid stimulus\nand not doing Covid stimulus,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240960,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like how medical scientists compare\na placebo group to a treatment group."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245880,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this is true for big physical systems\nas well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249640,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You kind of put the Earth in a laboratory\nto study the impact of greenhouse gases"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253400,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on global warming."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254800,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You cannot put stars in a lab to study\nhow black holes are formed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259360,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, you see in all of science"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261480,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the bigger the system gets,\nthe more difficult science becomes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 265200,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the easier it is to criticize\nthe results of studies that use"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269520,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mathematical models or statistical models,\nor quasi experimental methods,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273920,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rather than real gold\nstandard controlled experiments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277720,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, even though natural scientists\nalso struggle with this problem,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281520,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I do agree with Gary\nthat even for these big systems,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284880,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "social systems on average\nare even more difficult to study"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288880,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than very big natural systems\nlike the solar system, for two reasons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293360,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first reason is that social systems\nsimply tend to be more complex"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297360,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than physical systems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298880,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After all, atoms or chemicals\ndo not have a brain that can plan"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302160,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ahead, learn, and react to its environment\nlike humans do."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306120,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, while economists\nmay do experiments in a laboratory,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 308920,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just as chemists or biologists do,\nthe results from small scale controlled"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313000,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "human experiments are far less likely\nto hold up in a real world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316880,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "setting than those from a small scale\nchemical experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321080,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, on the big scale,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322400,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while macro economists are using more\nand more experiments or so-called quasi"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326520,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "experimental methods that mimic\nexperiments, they still have to deal with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330360,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the fact that humans are inherently less\npredictable than atoms or even animals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335960,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To make matters worse,\nthere's this second reason"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338640,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why social sciences struggle,\nwhich is that unlike natural scientists,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342640,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "social scientists are part of the system\nthat they study."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346240,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, about Gary's Covid economy,\nmost economists predicted that the world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351080,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would face a big recession or depression\nwith deflation rather than inflation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356400,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, because the government\nactually listened to these economists,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360840,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they started massive stimulus programs\nto avert a recession with deflation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366160,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But they then created an economic boom\nwith lots of inflation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370560,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a problem that natural scientists\ndo not have to deal with."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374520,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example,\nan asteroid does not change its course"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376920,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because some physicists predict\nthat it will crash into a planet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381400,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So Gary is right\neconomics is not a physical science,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 384800,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "making it harder to do experiments that\nthen help generate reliable predictions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390480,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why on this channel,\nI often try to stress that while I do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393720,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "make some macroeconomic predictions,\nthey will typically not be very reliable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399840,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This brings us to Gary's second\nclaim in that clip."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403720,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's watch it again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405120,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that is why banks pay millions\nof pounds a year to good predictors,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408720,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because that's the best way to tell\nwho is a good economist,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411240,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because we can't do physical experiments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413040,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it drives me mad that these economists\nwho make policy and protect policy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417480,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that protects them and their class\nand the rich don't even accept"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422280,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when somebody consistently predicts them,\nthey won't even listen to them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 425640,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It drives me mad."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426840,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, this is where Gary and I\ntruly, completely disagree."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430960,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I say nobody can make really good\nmacroeconomic predictions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434040,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the system is so complex and\nwe can't study it’s dynamics in the lab."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 438360,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Gary says, hold on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440400,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Banks paid people like me a lot of money\nto make these types of predictions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444680,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I got rich."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445800,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you academic economists did not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449040,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So why don't economists\nlisten to people like Gary?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452720,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the reason it is going to sound\nreally brutal, but actually is because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456520,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "economists have found that they cannot\nactually distinguish professional traders"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460560,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like Gary from monkeys\nthrowing darts at a financial newspaper."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465600,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, let me explain."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466720,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And please don't take this personal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468080,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gary, I personally believe\nyou were a very skilled trader"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471160,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I look at your predictions on YouTube\nand they were pretty good."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475400,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You some point had six out of nine\nor something like that were correct."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478440,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gary, then to tell you about all the ones\nthat were correct a lot on this channel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482640,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But yeah, he also got some stuff wrong,\nlike saying house prices would go up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487040,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quite a bit further"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488360,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while they really didn't, and that Covid\nwould massively increase inequality,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492200,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while the data at least says that\nthat really was not the case."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495560,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Still six out of nine,\nthat's actually really good."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497760,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I said the system cannot be predicted,\nso you'd probably expect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501320,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gary would get about 50% or\nso of his predictions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504520,
    "dDurationMs": 800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 505320,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And he clearly got more than 50%\njust being a bit more right than wrong."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509880,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's enough to make you a millionaire\nin financial markets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 513480,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, the problem is simply\nthat if enough people"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 516720,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bet on markets every day,\nsome people will, yes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 520280,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inevitably, statistically, always do\nwell for a couple of years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524280,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why\nthere are actually serious experiments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 526960,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where professional traders\nlike Gary get beaten by animals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531160,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, there's a famous Wall Street\nJournal supervised experiment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 534680,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where a blindfolded monkey\nbeat professional traders."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538880,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To make matters worse, in 2012,\nprofessional traders"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541200,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like Gary were defeated by a cat\ndropping a mouse toys on the stock market."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 546600,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Suggestions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548040,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In an experiment that lasted a full year,\nand then more scientific experiments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 552000,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with hundreds of simulated monkeys\nselecting random stocks,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 555440,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about 10% of monkeys\noutperformed the market by over 940%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559840,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, professional traders are famously\nstruggling to outperform the market"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563840,
    "dDurationMs": 1160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565000,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So sure, Gary's predictions\ntrack record may seem impressive,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568840,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it could be his impressive skills\nas an economist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571640,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Absolutely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572680,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But at the end of the day,\nthere will always be some monkeys"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575400,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that are better at predicting\nthan professional traders like Gary"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578840,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or Ray Dalio or Cathie\nWood for that matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581920,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is why economists don't\neven accept"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585760,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when somebody consistently predicts them,\nthey won't even listen to them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589320,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And instead, economic theories\nneed to be able to predict the future."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 592880,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, but they also need to be able\nto explain hundreds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595920,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of years of economic history"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 597520,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the same time, and also be confirmed\nin quasi experimental studies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 601440,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is a much higher standard than\njust betting money on financial markets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 605280,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "going up or down for a couple of years,\nwhich, as we have seen,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 609200,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can be done by a lucky monkey as well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 612560,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So yeah, that was a very long response,\nI realize."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 616200,
    "dDurationMs": 840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So quick summary."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 617040,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, economic science is not as good\nor reliable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620280,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as most natural sciences\nbecause humans are unpredictable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 623640,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And to make matters worse,\nthey actually listen to economists,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627240,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which then makes economic predictions\nsometimes not come true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630800,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, some rich traders\nmake good predictions for years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 633720,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yes, it could be\nthat they're really good at economics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637560,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for us economists,\nwe cannot distinguish them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 640400,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from monkeys\nthrowing darts at a financial newspaper."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 643720,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is why economic theories\nhave to explain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646920,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the future and past\nand be confirmed in experiments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650240,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which economists are doing more\nand more often, which is great, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 656400,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Economics is getting more scientific."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658640,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But of course, there's still plenty\nthat economists"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 661880,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can genuinely be criticized about."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664680,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I will react to that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 666920,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After telling you about me getting three\nvery fair criticisms from my wife"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672720,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about me and my academic ways,\nand how today's video"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 675880,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sponsor Ekster helps me to address them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679240,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First,\nI am often criticized for ruining my look"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682080,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by having this giant wallet\nstick out of my pants."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684920,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ekster fixed this by sending me\nthis super convenient slim wallet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 689880,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this even slimmer card holder\nwhere cards pop out just like this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696160,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and where both are RFID protected,\ncome with lifetime"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 699360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "warranty, and there are several colors\nfor him and her."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702760,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Second, I've been criticized\nfor losing my stuff way too often,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 706200,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "potentially due\nto thinking about economics all the time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708960,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "An extra fix this with this handy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 711720,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "finder card that I now have in my wallet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 715240,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Third, I don't know why,\nbut my clothes packing skills are terrible"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 718520,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Ekster fixed this with this super\nhandy travel vacuum kit, which is great."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723600,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I will use it to compress my kids\nholiday clothes for a vacation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 727720,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because it keeps our bag super organized."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730560,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If any of these problems\nsound recognizable,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732800,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or if you were looking for a great gift\nfor the holidays, I'm super"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 735960,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "happy to say\nthat I have secured a 10% discount"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739040,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on top of a sitewide 55% discount\nfor all Money and Macro viewers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 744120,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just scan this QR code\nor go to partners.ekster.com/moneymacro"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 749600,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and fill in my promo code\nmacro at checkout,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753080,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after which we can move\nto the second major criticism people"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 757240,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like to lob at economics, which is that\neconomic models are terribly outdated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 762880,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, Alejandro told me\nthis was a clip from famous Bitcoin"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766920,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "investor Michael Saylor on the Lex Fridman\npodcast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 771000,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's have a look."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772040,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, I think that if we're going\nto want to really make"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775200,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "any scientific progress in economics,\nwe have to apply much,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 779760,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much more computationally intensive\nand richer forms of mathematics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784560,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you want to describe\nhow anything works"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 788160,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the real world, you have to start\nwith the concept of feedback."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 791760,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If I double the price of something,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 794440,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "demand will fall and attempts to to create\nsupply will increase"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 799440,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and there will be a delay\nbefore the capacity increases."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804240,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There'll be an end demand change,\nand there will be rippling effects"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 808320,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "throughout every other segment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809640,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the economy, downstream\nand upstream of such thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 813360,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it's kind of common sense."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 815600,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But most economics,\nmost classical economics, it's always,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819200,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know, taught with linear models,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 822280,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know, fairly simplistic linear models."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824880,
    "dDurationMs": 280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 825160,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That was a really interesting clip\nby Michael Saylor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 827360,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because for me\nit really encompasses ignorance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 831000,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is a critique\nthat people often have about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 834720,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "economic models\nis, look, they are too simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 838480,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're oversimplified."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 839800,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And actually, that point I agree with."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 841800,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I did my thesis on this very thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 844880,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I explored this new modeling\ntechnique exactly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 847400,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Something that Michael Saylor here\nis talking about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 849920,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "agent based models,\ncomputational agent based models."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 852480,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I made these massive models."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854400,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I coded them up,\nsimulated thousands of households"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 859080,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and hundreds of firms and tens of banks\nand the government and central bank."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 865080,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what I found is that\nthis is a really useful technique"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 869880,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to study some phenomena in macroeconomics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 873560,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but there's also a huge downside to it,\nand that is that the more complex"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 878320,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your model is, the more difficult\nit is to actually understand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 881440,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what's going on in the model, and the more\nlikely there will be some bugs,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 886080,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just as you see in computer games,\nwith these models."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 888960,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So to that point, I think Saylor is right\nwith this critique is very old."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 893720,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I started my Phd"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 896160,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a lot of years ago, and in the meantime,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 899440,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know, central banks are working now\nwith a lot of these agent based"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 903040,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "computational models alongside\nmany different modeling techniques,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 906280,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "alongside the more simple models\nthat Saylor here is critiquing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 910920,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But then for his critique\nabout these more simple models,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 914320,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I don't think he knows\nwhat he's talking about."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916640,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He's saying, look,\nthese models don't have feedback"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920120,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like their general equilibrium models."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 922960,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This what they call typically dynamics\nstochastic general equilibrium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 926360,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "models are the most popular models\nin macroeconomics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 929280,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're dynamic okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 931040,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're talking about equilibrium,\nabout supply demand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 934520,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "being in in balance\nwith each other in equilibrium,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 937920,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and how they react\nif they become out of equilibrium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 941160,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or if something happens to that,\nand then they react back"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 944360,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and forth with each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 945360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And Michael Saylor is saying,\noh, economists don't follow this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 948360,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is just a basic mistake like they do\nwhile it it's at the heart of these"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 952840,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relatively simple models is supply\nand demand is feedback."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 958040,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they are dynamic\nthat he's saying they're linear models."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 960880,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're not"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 961920,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dynamic stochastic general equilibrium\nmodels are not linear models okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 965360,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're dynamic, but I think I know\nwhere the confusion comes from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 968920,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because some of these models\nare solved in a linear way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 972120,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's a mathematical trick\nto make solving them easier."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 976000,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I think that's\nwhat he's talking about."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 977520,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But honestly, this guy doesn't know\nmuch about economic models."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 982480,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And he got very rich investing in Bitcoin."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 984840,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I'm not gonna criticize him for that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 987200,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But economic models no."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 989080,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Someone who does know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 990360,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a lot about economic models though,\nand economics in general is Professor"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 994240,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Richard Werner,\nwhich I think the next clip is from."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 999240,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well,\nthe reason is that the the economists"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1002400,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "follow this theory that banks are just\nfinancial intermediaries, that just,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1006600,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know, gather deposits here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1008240,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do the analysis credit, in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1011080,
    "dDurationMs": 440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "analysis, you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1011520,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "know, risk assessment and, and all that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1014520,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then they allocate the funds\nand invest or they just take a percentage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1019120,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're a -\nSo so they're intermediaries. Yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1021800,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that's wrong.\nThat's not what they are."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1024280,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's it's one theory of banking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1026080,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's still the one that still dominant\nin all the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1028640,
    "dDurationMs": 920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "text books the leading journals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1029560,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They still use that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1031640,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but actually, if you look into it, you\nrealize there's three theories of banking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1035360,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A second theory, slightly older,\nthat was dominant until the 1960s,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1039920,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so-called fractional reserve theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1041440,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you may have heard\nthis fractional reserve, banking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1045320,
    "dDurationMs": 640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What is that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1045960,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well,\nthis theory says this part is similar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1049080,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each bank is a financial intermediary."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1050720,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It just collects deposits and then does\nthe analysis lends out the money."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1055280,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in aggregate, as banks interact,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1059720,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's money creation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1061840,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, and that's where students, yes,\nshould have bricked up money creation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1064760,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They even talk about money multiplier."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1066560,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1068680,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's the second theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1070160,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now there's a third theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1072280,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that one had been made out\nto be a wacky conspiracy theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1077320,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, but it is the one that was more\nor less"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1080600,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quite widely known\nuntil about a century ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1084800,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's the credit\ncreation theory of banking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1087160,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this one says"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1089200,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "banks are not financial intermediaries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1091720,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Banks are special."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1093720,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They have a unique power\nthat no other player"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1098680,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the economy has,\nand that is the power to create money."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1103160,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay.\nSo this critique,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1105320,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I fundamentally really agree\nwith in the sense that I do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1110480,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "focus on this channel very much on bank\nmoney creation in many, many videos."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1114600,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, he's right,\nthat many standard macroeconomic models"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1119160,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "don't have banks that create money,\nwhich seems like a giant oversight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1123440,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right? That seems super important."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1125840,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the problem here is kind of similar\nto what Michael"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1129560,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Saylor said here is that, like,\nyou can't model everything, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1133640,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you need to simplify somewhere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1136560,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And after in this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1138320,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in these models, these DSD models,\nthey don't have banks that create money."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1142800,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now after a financial crisis,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1146320,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there are also many DHC models\nthat do have bank money creation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1150440,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and do have these things that Professor\nWerner here is talking about."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1155360,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I think his critique, there's\ndefinitely truth in it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1159800,
    "dDurationMs": 840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bank money creation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1160640,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I've been promoting this super important\nfor the economy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1164120,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more important than most economists\nI think, recognize."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1168320,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But many economists do recognize this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1171400,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Central banks do recognize this, \nand they're more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1174920,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and more models\nthat do actually include this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1177080,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I think Professor Richard Werner,\nI know I've read his books,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1181200,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he's been criticizing this,\nthis type of criticism"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1185240,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for a long time, and I think by\nnow is a little bit outdated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1189240,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there are a lot of models that have\nthis, but definitely read his books."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1193520,
    "dDurationMs": 1160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're very interesting."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1194680,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is important. So yeah, absolutely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1198360,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there's more there's more wrong\nwith macroeconomic models."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1202040,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's see our friend Gary again, who"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1205400,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think the next clip is from the models\nwhich we study at universities nowadays."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1212480,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the big simplifications"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1214920,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that there is no inequality\nin the model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1219920,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, it's more than just that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1221640,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is no inequality in the model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1225760,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is only one person in the model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1229280,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So these models are what they call\nrepresentative agent models."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1234600,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So rather than looking at 6\nor 7 billion people in the world,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1238480,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or like 66 million people in the UK,\nor 300 million people in the US,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1243280,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they say to make the model simpler,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1246360,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we are just going to look at one\nrepresentative person."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1250560,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the average person\nin the whole economy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1253760,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So all you care about is averages, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1255560,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You're just taking one average person."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1256920,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And of course if we change\nthe distribution, if I take some wealth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1260040,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from you and give it to Bill gates,\nor if I take some wealth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1264000,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from Rishi Sunak and give it to you,\nthat changes the distribution."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1267520,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it doesn't change the average."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1269480,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So basically, once you build this model,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1272040,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which only looks\nat the representative agent,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1274960,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is the average,\nwhich is the aggregate, it's not only"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1278600,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that there is no inequality in the model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1281880,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is not even any possibility\nfor inequality model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1285400,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are models of averages. Theorem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1288640,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are models of aggregates,\nwhich is why"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1292520,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when modern economists\nyou've been to these elite universities"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1296600,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "think about the economy,\nthey tend to think about them in terms of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1300440,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "averages or aggregate,\nso that they're obsessed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1302720,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the big aggregate\nmeasurements of the economy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1305360,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, GDP\nis, of course, the classic one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1308840,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unemployment,\ninflation, central bank interest"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1312560,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rates, level of government\nspending, level of government taxation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1316560,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are things which you can measure\non an aggregate economy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1320000,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they're nothing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1321200,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to do with how is one person\naffected versus another person."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1325120,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So okay again\nwe see this critique standard simplified"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1328400,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "models don't have a realistic feature\nor a critical feature like inequality."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1333200,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, the models that I previously made\ndid have this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1336560,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They were very complex.\nThey also had bank money creation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1339240,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But my model was really hard to study"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1341120,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "precisely\nbecause it had so many, so many features."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1344920,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore,\nmost economists make specialized variants"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1348400,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the models that are in the standard."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1351560,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, economists like Chicago\nprofessor Greg Kaplan do study"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1355640,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inequality in these types of models\nthat Gary is talking about."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1358880,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they just do it by expanding it,\ncreating a variation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1362600,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then they do model wealth inequality\nbetween households."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1366320,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this critique is not entirely true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1368680,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there's really actually a lot of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1372360,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "very well known economists\nthat even some of them won Nobel Prizes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1376240,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Angus Deaton, there's also Joseph\nStiglitz, Toni Atkinson."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1380360,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Piketty is also very well known\nthat do study inequality."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1383200,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in fact, this literature has really\nexploded over the past six years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1388440,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I don't think this critique\nis completely true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1391760,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Gary's right\nthat a standard model does not have this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1395480,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you are just doing a bachelors\nor a masters in economics like Gary did,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1401280,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you will not encounter\nthese types of models"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1403280,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then you won't learn about inequality\ntoo much."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1406200,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's a fair critique."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1408080,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think that is a problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1409760,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So yeah, there's absolutely\nsome truth here, but I think what"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1413840,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we've seen now with these three clips\nis that,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1416960,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "yeah, many models are wrong"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1419880,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and many don't have crucial features."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1422320,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the problem is also that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1423360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you include all of these features,\nthen the model is too big."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1426440,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You don't understand it anymore."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1427760,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is just something"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1429040,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that economists and and scientists overall\nI think have not figured out yet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1434160,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you are\ngoing to study economics in university,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1437280,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then yeah, you will not see many of this\nsuper important features."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1441800,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You will only see the simple models,\nwhich gets us to the third"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1445640,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "type of criticism, which I'm\ngoing to react to today, which is that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1449360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "economic education is bad."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1453080,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Professor Steve Keen,\nwhom I actually met a couple of times,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1455840,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I did a visit to the university\nthat he was at the time, King's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1459520,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "University of London during my BSD,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1461160,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I think Steve King\ndoes some really good modeling,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1464040,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he made some really interesting\nsoftware for students called Minsky"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1467720,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that I absolutely encourage people\nto tinker with if they want to understand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1471600,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "macroeconomics, but that does not mean\nthat I agree with Keen on Everything."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1475640,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's see what he has to say."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1477360,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What you learn is an obsolete technology."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1479600,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Learning economics at a university\nis like learning."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1482040,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's all like astronomy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1484160,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The centric equilibrium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1486400,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "epicycles being added to make your models\nfit the data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1489280,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it's not that economics\nis not a discipline worth deeply studying,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1493400,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's that the university education around\nthat kind of so bad is bad."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1497080,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, I'd say learn system dynamics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1499280,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "do a course in system the dynamics\nwhich you can apply in any field,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1502720,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then apply\nwhat you learn out of system dynamics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1505920,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the issues of economics,\nif that's what interests you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1508640,
    "dDurationMs": 480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1509120,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So here I disagree with Steve Keene. Yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1512160,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "An economics education is too often about\njust doing some simple math"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1516040,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rather than studying economics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1518120,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this can be explains."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1520880,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You see, education is very conservative."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1523520,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It takes time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1524560,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Research is actually quite a lot further."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1527080,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have banks\nand we have inequality in research."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1530320,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for teachers to implement\nall of this in their teaching program"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1533960,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is actually pretty difficult because\nteachers are under a lot of pressure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1537680,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Typically in economics\nthey're not so well-paid,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1540520,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they have so many students\nand so much grading to do."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1543920,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And now, as a conclusion,\nvery often students don't see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1549440,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all the best things that the economics\nprofession is working on right now."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1554240,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But honestly, Keynes\nmodels are not perfect either."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1557840,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They don't have a lot\nof realistic features"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1560280,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like actual humans in their modeled\nand how they would behave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1564760,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So again,\nI think the same problem comes back."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1569480,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Economics is not perfect,\nbut it's also, as we discussed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1573400,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the start of this video,\nbecause the system,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1576320,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "especially the macroeconomic system\nthat economists are trying to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1579080,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "study, is just so massive\nand not fully explored yet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1583840,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so, yeah,\nbecause economists have a lot of work"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1587120,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to do and an economics\neducation is not perfect, but definitely"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1590960,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "do study it in university\nI did, and I loved it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1593880,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you will too. You will learn a lot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1596040,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think. Conclusion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1597920,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So yeah, that was my response\nto these three types of critiques."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1602320,
    "dDurationMs": 280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Critique."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1602600,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number one,\neconomics is not a hard or real science."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1607040,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, it's not a hard science."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1608960,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is real science, I'd argue."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1610400,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it's a social science."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1612200,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Social systems are more complex\nthan natural systems"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1615000,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because humans are more complex."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1616560,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And on top of that, social scientists\nmay influence the system that they're in,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1620680,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in validating their predictions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1622640,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And on top of that, just as with climate\nscience or studying planets, the bigger"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1626960,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a system gets, the less easy\nit is to study them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1630520,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through at least a gold standard\nof science controlled experiments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1634120,
    "dDurationMs": 640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That being said,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1634760,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "economists are trying to do more\nand more experiments are even featured."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1637960,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A proper macroeconomic experiment\non this channel last year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1641120,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I'm actually very excited\nfor the future of economics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1645640,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you'll hear all about it\non this channel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1647640,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even if critiques like economic models\naren't terribly outdated,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1652040,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have some truth to them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1653720,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I somewhat agree with these."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1655480,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, most economic\nmodels are very much oversimplified,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1659320,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but as I have seen firsthand,\nwe don't have a perfect alternative yet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1663960,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, I've made some super advanced\nsimulation models"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1666880,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Michael Saylor would love,\nbut these had their own problems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1671120,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They were very difficult to track\nwhat was going on with them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1674840,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1675800,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so I think there's a place\nfor many different types of models."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1679520,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there are."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1681080,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when Keynes says don't study\neconomics, it's a waste of time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1685520,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I really disagree."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1686600,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, you should be careful where you study\neconomics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1689960,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I recommend that you pick a department\nthat's known to be somewhat progressive,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1694640,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scientifically speaking, where they teach\nmultiple schools of thought,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1697760,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "teach them economic history, and focus\non empirical economics, where really"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1701760,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all the action is these days alongside\nthese standard mathematical models."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1705800,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And of course, on the side,\nalways watch this channel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1708680,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But yeah, that is my take. Do you agree?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1711200,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let me know in the comments."
    } ]
